# 8. Networking – Subnet Mask

A subnet mask works with an IP address to identify the network portion and host portion of an IP address.

Example:

```text
IP Address:
192.168.1.10

Subnet Mask:
255.255.255.0
```

The subnet mask helps determine which portion represents the network and which portion represents the host.

---

# 9. Private and Public IP Addresses

## Private IP

A private IP address is used within a private/local network and is not directly routable across the public Internet.

Common private IPv4 ranges include:

```text
10.0.0.0/8

172.16.0.0 – 172.31.255.255

192.168.0.0/16
```

## Public IP

A public IP address is globally routable and is used for communication across the public Internet.

Public IPv4 connectivity is commonly provided through an ISP or organization.

---

# 10. NAT

NAT stands for Network Address Translation.

NAT translates IP addressing between different network contexts and commonly allows devices using private IPv4 addresses to access the Internet through public IPv4 connectivity.

Example:

```text
Private IP
192.168.1.10
      ↓
     NAT
      ↓
Public IP
      ↓
Internet
```

